# Raw source data is never committed: ~1.6 GB of DLA FLIS archives, several over
# GitHub's 100 MB file limit. It is published as assets on the `data-v1` release
# and restored with `scripts/fetch_data.sh`. Provenance: docs/DATA_PROVENANCE.md
data/
*.zip
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.parquet
# ...except the ML training set, which is small, generated, and the thing a
# reviewer most wants to open. See datasets/README.md.
!datasets/training/*.csv
# models/* not models/ — an excluded DIRECTORY cannot be re-entered by a later
# negation, so the pattern has to exclude its contents instead.
models/*
# ...but the fitted scorer ships. It is 17 KB of named coefficients, not a
# 128 MB checkpoint, and without it a fresh clone silently falls back to the
# deterministic path and reports uncalibrated scores with no sign anything is
# missing. Retraining it needs the corpus and ~50 s; committing it costs nothing.
!models/scorer/
!models/scorer/*.json
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
node_modules/

# secrets and local environment — never committed
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# editor / agent tooling that is personal to one machine
.claude/

# frontend
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/

# local working database — regenerated on API startup (create_all + seed).
# A clean, session-free snapshot ships at db/sangam_seed.db instead.
sangam.db
sangam.db-wal
sangam.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
